1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,084
Here's what happened this week.

2
00:00:02,784 --> 00:00:06,134
In Kuwait, a drone strike killed two Italian engineers.

3
00:00:06,711 --> 00:00:08,268
Italy blames Iran.

4
00:00:08,776 --> 00:00:11,870
Tehran denies it, and suggests it was a false flag.

5
00:00:12,570 --> 00:00:16,068
We'll also look at a strike claim in Saudi Arabia

6
00:00:16,068 --> 00:00:19,567
that moved oil prices, and another night of missiles over Ukraine.

7
00:00:20,267 --> 00:00:23,339
Plus an ISIS attack in Syria, deadly strikes

8
00:00:23,339 --> 00:00:26,411
in Gaza, and a record Ebola outbreak in Congo.

9
00:00:27,111 --> 00:00:28,754
Let's start in Kuwait.

10
00:00:29,403 --> 00:00:33,254
A drone struck an air defence detection station, where two

11
00:00:33,254 --> 00:00:37,105
Italian technicians working for the defence company Rheinmetall were killed.

12
00:00:37,805 --> 00:00:40,770
Kuwait's defence ministry says two other people,

13
00:00:40,770 --> 00:00:43,735
a Kuwaiti and a Pakistani national, were injured.

14
00:00:44,435 --> 00:00:48,254
Italy's foreign minister, Antonio Tajani, says the drones were Iranian, and

15
00:00:48,254 --> 00:00:52,073
that the drone used in the attack was made in Iran.

16
00:00:52,719 --> 00:00:56,143
Kuwait says the attack violated a UN Security

17
00:00:56,143 --> 00:00:59,567
Council resolution, and has invoked its right to self-defence.

18
00:01:00,267 --> 00:01:01,931
Iran denies any role.

19
00:01:02,490 --> 00:01:07,279
A military spokesman said its armed forces had carried out no operations in

20
00:01:07,279 --> 00:01:12,068
the region, and suggested the attack was a false flag, meant to escalate tensions.

21
00:01:12,670 --> 00:01:17,043
Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi told his Italian counterpart that Iran

22
00:01:17,043 --> 00:01:21,417
was not involved, and offered a joint investigation with Kuwait.

23
00:01:22,117 --> 00:01:25,551
Who launched the drones has not been independently verified.

24
00:01:26,751 --> 00:01:30,506
Next, to Saudi Arabia, where Yemen's Houthi movement says

25
00:01:30,506 --> 00:01:34,261
it has struck Ras Tanura, the country's largest oil refinery.

26
00:01:34,961 --> 00:01:38,086
The group says the attack started fires, and satellite

27
00:01:38,086 --> 00:01:41,211
images showed thick black smoke rising over the site.

28
00:01:41,911 --> 00:01:44,802
The Saudi-led coalition says its air

29
00:01:44,802 --> 00:01:47,693
defences intercepted four drones over Ras Tanura.

30
00:01:48,294 --> 00:01:51,430
It has not confirmed any damage to the refinery itself.

31
00:01:52,130 --> 00:01:55,416
In Riyadh, a tower in the financial district was hit.

32
00:01:56,050 --> 00:01:59,186
Saudi civil defence says eleven people were wounded.

33
00:01:59,689 --> 00:02:02,974
It was the second strike on the same tower in less than a week.

34
00:02:03,674 --> 00:02:05,914
Oil prices jumped after the claim.

35
00:02:06,490 --> 00:02:08,868
The coalition has promised a firm response,

36
00:02:08,868 --> 00:02:11,247
and the Houthis are threatening more attacks.

37
00:02:12,447 --> 00:02:15,210
To Ukraine, where Russia launched another large

38
00:02:15,210 --> 00:02:17,972
overnight barrage of ballistic missiles and drones.

39
00:02:18,672 --> 00:02:22,406
Ukraine says its air defences shot down eighty-seven of them.

40
00:02:23,106 --> 00:02:27,607
In Kharkiv, a drone hit a residential high-rise, killing a man and a woman.

41
00:02:28,154 --> 00:02:30,618
A third person was killed when another

42
00:02:30,618 --> 00:02:33,082
strike hit an educational building in the city.

43
00:02:33,782 --> 00:02:37,121
Across the country, the public broadcaster Suspilne reports

44
00:02:37,121 --> 00:02:40,460
at least seven people killed and fifty-eight injured.

45
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:44,637
The attack came after Vladimir Putin warned of

46
00:02:44,637 --> 00:02:48,114
retaliation for Ukrainian strikes on Russian energy facilities.

47
00:02:49,314 --> 00:02:52,376
In north-east Syria, the Islamic State group attacked

48
00:02:52,376 --> 00:02:55,437
an internal security building in the city of Hassakeh.

49
00:02:56,137 --> 00:02:58,942
Syrian state media says two members of the

50
00:02:58,942 --> 00:03:01,748
security forces were killed, and five were injured.

51
00:03:02,448 --> 00:03:04,880
Officials say all four attackers died.

52
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:08,486
Two were killed in clashes, and two blew themselves up.

53
00:03:09,186 --> 00:03:12,141
It's a reminder that ISIS cells remain active in

54
00:03:12,141 --> 00:03:15,096
the region, years after the group lost its territory.

55
00:03:16,296 --> 00:03:18,813
In Gaza, hospital officials say

56
00:03:18,813 --> 00:03:21,330
Israeli strikes overnight killed eight Palestinians.

57
00:03:22,030 --> 00:03:26,190
That came a day after nine people were reported killed in separate strikes.

58
00:03:26,890 --> 00:03:30,005
A ceasefire has been in place since October

59
00:03:30,005 --> 00:03:33,120
2025, but deadly strikes have repeatedly tested it.

60
00:03:33,633 --> 00:03:35,894
Israel has said earlier strikes were

61
00:03:35,894 --> 00:03:38,155
responses to militant attacks on its troops.

62
00:03:39,355 --> 00:03:42,982
And finally, to the Democratic Republic of Congo, where an

63
00:03:42,982 --> 00:03:46,609
Ebola outbreak has become the largest the country has ever recorded.

64
00:03:47,309 --> 00:03:52,695
As of November seventeenth, Europe's disease control agency counted eleven thousand, five

65
00:03:52,695 --> 00:03:58,082
hundred and four confirmed cases, and five thousand, six hundred and thirty deaths.

66
00:03:58,782 --> 00:04:03,027
The outbreak, caused by the Bundibugyo strain of the virus, began in May.

67
00:04:03,668 --> 00:04:07,913
UNICEF says children make up around twenty-eight percent of confirmed cases.

68
00:04:08,613 --> 00:04:12,688
Africa CDC says the outbreak is still not under control,

69
00:04:12,688 --> 00:04:16,762
with conflict, late detection and stretched health services slowing the response.

70
00:04:17,962 --> 00:04:19,114
That's the week.

71
00:04:19,715 --> 00:04:21,913
But one question still hangs over it.

72
00:04:22,613 --> 00:04:26,559
Italy and Kuwait say the drone that killed two Italians was Iranian.

73
00:04:27,093 --> 00:04:29,098
Tehran says it was a false flag.

74
00:04:29,798 --> 00:04:31,803
Some in Iran have gone further.

75
00:04:32,407 --> 00:04:36,397
Mohammad Marandi, a former adviser to Iran's nuclear negotiators,

76
00:04:36,397 --> 00:04:40,386
claimed Ukraine could be behind it, but offered no evidence.

77
00:04:40,942 --> 00:04:43,716
Ukraine has sent military specialists to the

78
00:04:43,716 --> 00:04:46,489
Gulf to help defend against Iranian drones.

79
00:04:47,189 --> 00:04:49,802
Italy's foreign minister points out that

80
00:04:49,802 --> 00:04:52,416
many pro-Iranian militias operate in the region.

81
00:04:53,116 --> 00:04:55,036
So who really launched that drone?

82
00:04:55,655 --> 00:04:57,938
Iran, a group it backs, or someone

83
00:04:57,938 --> 00:05:00,221
trying to drag Europe deeper into this conflict?

84
00:05:00,828 --> 00:05:04,369
Until there's an independent investigation, we may not know.

85
00:05:05,069 --> 00:05:07,010
Tell us what you think in the comments.

86
00:05:07,659 --> 00:05:10,518
And subscribe, so you don't miss next week's episode.
